WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:17.287
"What?" Cole staring at Kyle.

2
00:00:17.307 --> 00:00:19.027
"No way!"

3
00:00:19.448 --> 00:00:20.068
Maggie said.

4
00:00:20.088 --> 00:00:24.570
"Does Lauren really want Coach Phillips to kick Cole out of tryouts?"

5
00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:29.052
"That's what I just said," Kyle said with another smirk.

6
00:00:30.124 --> 00:00:33.506
He took one more sip of his sports drink, and then wandered away.

7
00:00:34.866 --> 00:00:35.867
Cole looked upset.

8
00:00:35.887 --> 00:00:38.328
"I have to go talk to the coach!

9
00:00:39.528 --> 00:00:41.729
I have to beg him to give me another chance!"

10
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.010
"Wait a minute, Cole," said Henry.

11
00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:48.652
"Everyone knows that Kyle likes to cause trouble.

12
00:00:49.792 --> 00:00:51.533
What if he's just trying to make you worry?"

13
00:00:52.654 --> 00:00:53.374
Maggie nodded.

14
00:00:53.394 --> 00:00:57.716
"He's probably upset because you're doing better than him in the tryouts.

15
00:00:58.848 --> 00:01:00.689
He could be another one of our suspects!"

16
00:01:02.209 --> 00:01:03.829
"She's right," Henry said.

17
00:01:03.849 --> 00:01:07.750
"Did you notice that Kyle was sipping a sports drink?

18
00:01:08.891 --> 00:01:10.251
I'm pretty sure it was grape."

19
00:01:11.411 --> 00:01:12.892
"Really?" Maggie said.

20
00:01:12.912 --> 00:01:14.752
"That proves it!

21
00:01:15.653 --> 00:01:18.333
Kyle must have poured the grape drink on the towel.

22
00:01:19.294 --> 00:01:22.454
Then he dragged it through an anthill to try to scare Daisy away.

23
00:01:23.495 --> 00:01:25.735
He probably framed Cole for the frogs too!"

24
00:01:27.236 --> 00:01:27.956
Cole shrugged.

25
00:01:29.136 --> 00:01:30.237
"I guess it's possible.

26
00:01:31.318 --> 00:01:33.419
Kyle really wants the spot on the team.

27
00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:38.022
He's been teasing me all day, saying I'm too young and stuff like that."

28
00:01:38.042 --> 00:01:39.963
"Case closed!"

29
00:01:40.344 --> 00:01:41.184
Maggie exclaimed.

30
00:01:41.204 --> 00:01:43.146
"Let's go tell the coach!"

31
00:01:43.166 --> 00:01:45.627
"Wait," Henry said.

32
00:01:46.708 --> 00:01:48.629
As usual Maggie was rushing things.

33
00:01:48.649 --> 00:01:52.092
"The case isn't closed yet.

34
00:01:53.272 --> 00:01:55.034
We don't know for sure that Kyle did it.

35
00:01:56.154 --> 00:01:58.316
What if he's telling the truth about what he heard?

36
00:01:59.504 --> 00:02:01.566
Lauren was already one of our suspects.

37
00:02:02.887 --> 00:02:06.509
Maybe she wants to get Cole kicked out because he insulted her yesterday."

38
00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:08.551
Cole made a face.

39
00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:13.494
"Yeah, my big mouth sure got me in trouble with her," he admitted.

40
00:02:13.514 --> 00:02:16.977
"I tried to apologize, but she wouldn't listen."

41
00:02:18.478 --> 00:02:22.721
"Maybe we should go ask Coach Phillips if what Kyle said is true," Henry said.

42
00:02:22.741 --> 00:02:26.844
"If it is, then Lauren should be our main suspect.

43
00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:29.421
Otherwise it should be Kyle."

44
00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:32.741
Cole looked around the pool area for the coach.

45
00:02:33.822 --> 00:02:34.942
"He must still be inside.

46
00:02:35.902 --> 00:02:36.342
Let's go!"

47
00:02:37.803 --> 00:02:40.664
Henry, Cole, and Maggie headed toward the pool building.

48
00:02:41.744 --> 00:02:44.645
Just as they reached the door, Lauren came out with Daisy.

49
00:02:45.685 --> 00:02:47.426
Lauren saw Cole and frowned.

50
00:02:47.446 --> 00:02:49.686
"Where are you going?"

51
00:02:50.106 --> 00:02:50.787
she demanded.

52
00:02:50.807 --> 00:02:53.207
"Inside," Cole said.

53
00:02:53.227 --> 00:02:55.468
"We need to talk to the coach."

54
00:02:56.896 --> 00:02:59.478
"You don't have time right now," Lauren said.

55
00:02:59.498 --> 00:03:03.220
"I'm in charge until Coach Phillips comes back outside.

56
00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.322
And I want everyone to run laps around the pool building.

57
00:03:08.343 --> 00:03:12.745
Now!" She raised her voice for the last part so everyone could hear.

58
00:03:12.765 --> 00:03:15.467
A few of the swimmers groaned.

59
00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:19.229
But she ordered them to put on their sneakers and start running.

60
00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:24.612
Henry and Maggie watched as the swimmers disappeared behind the pool building.

61
00:03:25.792 --> 00:03:28.815
Lauren jogged away with them, leaving the pool area deserted.

62
00:03:28.835 --> 00:03:34.159
"It makes me feel hot just watching people jog in this weather," Maggie said.

63
00:03:34.179 --> 00:03:36.461
"Let's go stand in the shade."

64
00:03:36.481 --> 00:03:41.846
"Okay." Henry followed her around the corner of the building.

65
00:03:42.947 --> 00:03:47.351
There was shade there from some large trees, and they could see some walking trails too.

66
00:03:48.472 --> 00:03:50.093
Henry tried to glance back at the pool.

67
00:03:51.194 --> 00:03:53.076
But he couldn't see it from where they were standing.

68
00:03:54.624 --> 00:03:57.505
"Lauren seems really mad at Cole," he said.

69
00:03:57.525 --> 00:04:02.467
"She made everyone jog so he couldn't go inside and talk to the coach.

70
00:04:03.588 --> 00:04:05.568
Do you think she guessed that we suspect her?"

71
00:04:05.588 --> 00:04:08.510
"Maybe," Maggie said.

72
00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:11.511
"But I still think Kyle could be the bad guy.

73
00:04:12.371 --> 00:04:13.952
He really wants to get on the team.

74
00:04:15.432 --> 00:04:18.133
Cole and Daisy are the only two people who might stop him.

75
00:04:19.294 --> 00:04:21.395
And the two pranks today were aimed at them."

76
00:04:21.415 --> 00:04:25.345
"We shouldn't forget about Tommy though," Henry said.

77
00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:28.748
"He was the one who gave Daisy that towel.

78
00:04:29.689 --> 00:04:31.690
That means he's still a suspect too."

79
00:04:33.152 --> 00:04:34.253
Maggie looked doubtful.

80
00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:36.895
"Cole thinks it couldn't be Tommy."

81
00:04:38.036 --> 00:04:40.318
Henry was about to answer when he heard a shout.

82
00:04:41.459 --> 00:04:42.560
It came from near the pool.

83
00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.182
"That sounded like Coach Phillips!"

84
00:04:45.583 --> 00:04:46.003
he said.

85
00:04:46.023 --> 00:04:47.484
"Let's go!"

86
00:04:48.545 --> 00:04:51.188
Around the corner the coach was staring into the pool.

87
00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:56.402
A few of the joggers, including Cole, had made it back to the building by then.

88
00:04:56.422 --> 00:04:58.443
"What's wrong, Coach?"

89
00:04:58.824 --> 00:04:59.464
Cole called.

90
00:05:00.565 --> 00:05:02.166
Coach Phillips pointed to the water.

91
00:05:02.186 --> 00:05:03.987
"The frogs!"

92
00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:05.167
he exclaimed.

93
00:05:05.187 --> 00:05:07.269
"They're in the pool again!"

94
00:05:11.671 --> 00:05:15.273
Henry gasped when he saw the buckets tipped over at the edge of the pool.

95
00:05:17.715 --> 00:05:19.736
The rest of the joggers appeared around the corner.

96
00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:24.123
When they saw what had happened, everyone started talking at once.

97
00:05:24.143 --> 00:05:27.145
"Quiet!" the coach hollered.

98
00:05:27.165 --> 00:05:29.707
"I want to know who did this!"

99
00:05:31.349 --> 00:05:32.369
Nobody said a word.

100
00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:37.494
Lauren hurried toward the edge of the pool and picked up something on the ground near the buckets.

101
00:05:38.635 --> 00:05:39.956
"Look!" she cried.

102
00:05:39.976 --> 00:05:43.959
"Whoever did it left a pair of flip-flops behind."

103
00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:47.402
She held up two blue-and-white flip-flops.

104
00:05:48.803 --> 00:05:49.904
Cole let out a gasp.

105
00:05:51.106 --> 00:05:52.268
"Those are mine!"

106
00:05:52.669 --> 00:05:53.431
he blurted out.
